# A quick ⌘T g i t ⏎ lost its first keys: the bar's panel was key at once, but its field took the keys three
# main-queue turns later. On the first open the keys went nowhere; on later ones the field editor still held the
# last session's text, the key was typed onto it, and the text the bar opened with then wiped it.
# cra://debug?commandBarType opens the bar and types into it in the same turn, as a quick typist's keys arrive.
# Each case uses its own letters, since expect-log reads the whole log.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=600 stalls50=8
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=start
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1
wait 2
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
# A real click on the page makes Cra the active app, so the bar's panel takes the keys.
click page-top
wait 1
# The first open: the field has never held the keys.
cra://debug?commandBarType=abc
expect-log command bar query: abc field: abc$
cra://dismiss
wait 1
# A later ⌘T, after a session that left text in the field.
cra://commandbar?query=hello
wait 1
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarType=xyz
expect-log command bar query: xyz field: xyz$
cra://dismiss
wait 1
# ⌘L: the typed keys replace the page's address the bar opens with.
cra://commandbar?query=again
wait 1
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarType=qrs&mode=edit
expect-log command bar query: qrs field: qrs$
reject-log command bar key: the bar doesn't hold the keys
cra://dismiss
